7 remaining, and Ohio answered Akron’s fourth-quarter rally to beat the Zips 28-20 on Tuesday night.","story":"AKRON, Ohio -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5167252/duncan-brune\" target=\"_new\">Duncan Brune</a> had a 91-yard touchdown run with 3:57 remaining, and Ohio answered Akron’s fourth-quarter rally to beat the Zips 28-20 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Akron took a 17-14 lead with 9:35 left when <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5084582/jordan-gant\" target=\"_new\">Jordan Gant</a> scored on a 1-yard run, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5198324/cibastian-broughton\" target=\"_new\">Cibastian Broughton</a> found <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5193341/marcel-williams\" target=\"_new\">Marcel Williams</a> for the two-point conversion.\n\n\r\n              The lead lasted 13 seconds.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5228762/nick-poulos\" target=\"_new\">Nick Poulos</a> hit <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5193110/dom-dorwart\" target=\"_new\">Dom Dorwart</a> for a 60-yard touchdown on Ohio’s next play to put the Bobcats back in front 21-17. Brune later broke free for his 91-yard score to give Ohio (7-2, 5-0 Mid-American Conference) an 11-point cushion.\n\n\r\n              Ohio’s defense provided the Bobcats’ only touchdown of the first half. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5125829/dj-walker\" target=\"_new\">DJ Walker</a> intercepted Broughton and returned it 45 yards for a score with nine seconds left in the first quarter, giving Ohio a 7-3 lead.\n\n\r\n              Poulos finished 12 of 20 for 197 yards and a touchdown and rushed for 45 yards and another score. Dorwart caught four passes for 108 yards.\n\n\r\n              Gant rushed for 112 yards and a touchdown for Akron (1-8, 0-5) while Broughton threw for 232 yards.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Ohio: At Miami (OH) next Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              Akron: Hosts Western Michigan next Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-04T03:43:46Z"}}